+#!/usr/bin/env node
+/**
+ * THE FOOT'S DECLARATION WITNESS (T9-W7 · CTRL-TAPE, the shape of CTRL-COST's `check-cost-face`).
+ *
+ * CI is browserless (O-12), so what CI can hold is the DECLARATION a measured row follows from.
+ * Each clause below is the load-bearing half of a row read on paint in the e2e estate.
+ *
+ * PASS 7 · KEYED ON SHAPE, NOT ON SPELLING (LAWS P6 §F). Pass 6's gate listed the props it
+ * forbade on three literal selectors and read one file per clause: fifteen one-line breaks the
+ * critic fed it stayed GREEN (`overflow: hidden` and `contain: paint` on the bar, a `:deep()`
+ * rule hiding the frame's svg, `overflow: clip` on the foot, `#card-foot` and the logical and
+ * shorthand pads), four of them erasing the frame on paint. This gate reads EVERY site a
+ * declaration can reach the foot from — every stylesheet and every SFC `<style>` block (a second
+ * block too), `index.html`, `public/**`, template `style`/`:style`/utility classes on the
+ * elements themselves and script style writes in the foot's owners — through the chair's ONE
+ * shape-census library (`lib/shape-census.mjs`, byte-identical to `pass7/instruments/`), keys
+ * on the SUBJECT COMPOUND (class or id, `:is()` arms, `:deep()` unwrapped) and WHITELISTS where
+ * pass 6 enumerated.
+ *
+ *   1 THE INSET   every site that sets the foot's bottom pad (`padding-bottom`,
+ *                 `padding-block-end`, `padding-block`, `padding`, any selector whose subject
+ *                 is `.card-foot` or `#card-foot`, `var()` resolved) spends
+ *                 `env(safe-area-inset-bottom)` ADDED to a net pad no smaller than its regime's
+ *                 swept floor (0.75rem dock, 1.125rem short landscape; the rail's note berth
+ *                 `max(3.5rem, env())`). No utility class, inline style or script write sets it.
+ *   2 THE LAYER   every site positioning the foot keeps it positioned, and every `z-index` on it
+ *                 is ≥ the card's (unpositioned it paints UNDER the card; coverage 0.00).
+ *   3 THE PEN     the bar's `HandDrawnOutline` carries the WELLS' four props, mounts whenever the
+ *                 bar mounts (no `v-if`/`v-show`/`style`/`:class` on it or on any element between
+ *                 it and `.action-bar`), every rule whose subject is `.bar-frame` declares only
+ *                 its layout, and NO rule that descends from the bar or the foot may reach the
+ *                 frame's subtree: its subject must positively name a class or tag the frame
+ *                 (`HandDrawnOutline`'s own template) cannot carry.
+ *   4 ONE HAND    no rule on the bar's own box (`.action-bar`, `.action-verbs`, the foot) draws
+ *                 an edge, lays a slab or touches the ink the frame's `currentColor` rides.
+ *   5 THE FLOOR   the confirm's answers take `min-width`/`min-height: var(--tap-floor)` BARE.
+ *   6 THE BAND    `.controls-card` spends `padding-top: var(--pin-band)`, `--pin-band` is a
+ *                 `calc()`, and nothing in src publishes it (or its dead sample `--card-pad-t`).
+ *   7 THE REGIME  ONE predicate per regime (LAWS P5, the berth law): the foot's short-landscape
+ *                 pad, the tongue's flank (`DrawerTab`) and the quick set's berth
+ *                 (`useLandscapeFlank`) key on the SAME query, the note berth's pad and its mount
+ *                 (`useNoteBerth`) on the same query, and no module but `useCoarsePointer.ts`
+ *                 mints a media ref (a per-mount listener restates a regime).
+ *   8 THE CLIP    no clip-bearing property on the frame's ancestry (`.bar-frame`, `.action-bar`,
+ *                 the foot, `.drawer-case`): `overflow` other than visible, `contain` with
+ *                 paint/layout/strict/content, `clip-path`, `clip`, `mask*`, `content-visibility`;
+ *                 on the bar, the foot and the frame also `filter`, `opacity`, `visibility`,
+ *                 `display: none|contents` — by any selector, utility class or inline style.
+ *
+ * `--self-test` feeds every plant in memory (no tree file is written) and requires each to RED
